window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>\"I don't dabble in fortune-telling. I give spoilers.\" — the Soaz. Arien desires to protect her warrior family, even if that means giving up her bond with Kole and spending the rest of her life in hiding. But when hordes of supernaturals start hunting her, she becomes convinced the only way to protect her found family is to surrender to the menacing Magister of Invicta. </p> <p>Forced to face the council and under Invicta’s scrutiny, Arien tests the political arena to regain control of her life. Her plans are thrown off course when her new protector, Kole, suddenly leaves, and the cruel and enigmatic Soaz invades her mind with cryptic messages about her bloodline and the aloof shifter territory called the Fringe. </p> <p>Arien is afraid that she is outmatched, and that the fate of not only her future but also that of the council and Invicta hangs in the balance. Alone and desperate, can Arien stop the evil threatening Invicta once more before she’s claimed by a monster? </p> <p>Glass Water is the second book in the Earthbounders series, a gripping tale of love, betrayal, and high stakes - in which dying in place of loved ones is a high possibility.</p>"; 
